I led the testing efforts for the Urban Routes carsharing application, focusing on functional validation across key environments (Google Chrome at 800x600 and Firefox at 1920x1080). 
This sprint's activities encompassed a thorough analysis of application designs and requirements, the strategic creation of detailed test documentation (including design and functionality checklists, and comprehensive test cases), rigorous test execution, and meticulous bug reporting using Jira.
The testing scope covered critical user flows such as reservation, payment method management, the booking process, and the car rental feature. 
The detailed findings, including checklists, test cases, and links to reported defects, are documented in the provided Google Sheets. 
This systematic approach ensured a structured evaluation of the application's quality and identified areas for potential improvement.
